---
import TextPage from "../layouts/TextPage.astro";
import siteConfig from "../../site.config";
---

<TextPage
  eyebrow="Privacy"
  title="Privacy, in plain English"
  description="What Lyrica reads, what stays on your PC, what leaves it, and how to disconnect an optional account link."
  updated={siteConfig.legal.updated}
>
  <div class="not-prose rounded-3xl border border-line bg-surface p-5 sm:p-6">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-accent">The short version</p>
    <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#c9c9d0]">
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-accent">✓</span>There are no ads, trackers or analytics cookies on this site by default.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-accent">✓</span>Lyrica does not run a server that records your listening history.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-accent">✓</span>Settings, lyric cache and credentials stay on your PC.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-accent">✓</span>The only routine network requests are lyric lookups, optional update checks and optional account features you turn on.</li>
      <li class="flex gap-2.5"><span class="text-accent">✓</span>Discord sign-in gates the download and issues one free key. It does not read your messages, friends or servers.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>What the app reads</h2>
  <p>
    Lyrica reads the current media session that Windows already exposes: the track title, artist,
    album, duration, playback state and position. That is how it knows what is playing in Spotify,
    Apple Music, Cider or any other player in the Windows media flyout. It does not hook into the
    player, read its database or ask for your music password.
  </p>

  <figure class="not-prose my-8 rounded-3xl border border-line bg-[#08080a] p-4 sm:p-6">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 760 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="data-flow-title data-flow-desc" class="w-full">
      <title id="data-flow-title">Where Lyrica's data goes</title>
      <desc id="data-flow-desc">Your player sends now-playing information to Lyrica on your PC. Settings, cache and credentials stay local. Optional lyric lookups and update checks leave the PC only when you use those features.</desc>
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="flow-accent" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="#ff5c8a" stop-opacity=".22" />
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="#ff5c8a" stop-opacity=".04" />
        </linearGradient>
        <marker id="arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="7" refY="4" orient="auto">
          <path d="M0 0 8 4 0 8Z" fill="#8a8a93" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <rect x="24" y="120" width="180" height="92" rx="20" fill="#111113" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,.12)" />
      <text x="114" y="153" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="600">Your player</text>
      <text x="114" y="174" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a8a93" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="10">Spotify, Apple Music, Cider</text>
      <text x="114" y="190" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a8a93" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="10">Windows media session</text>

      <rect x="286" y="82" width="200" height="168" rx="24" fill="url(#flow-accent)" stroke="rgba(255,92,138,.35)" />
      <text x="386" y="116" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-family="Inter Tight, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="700">Lyrica on your PC</text>
      <text x="386" y="140" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c9c9d0" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="10">Reads now-playing info</text>
      <text x="386" y="157" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c9c9d0" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="10">Draws lyrics locally</text>
      <text x="386" y="174" text-anchor="middle" fill="#c9c9d0" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="10">No listening history uploaded</text>
      <text x="386" y="210" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ff9dbb" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="10" font-weight="600">the centre of the diagram</text>

      <rect x="548" y="34" width="188" height="72" rx="18" fill="#111113" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,.12)" />
      <text x="642" y="63" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600">Stays on your PC</text>
      <text x="642" y="82" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a8a93" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="9.5">settings · cache · credentials</text>

      <rect x="548" y="128" width="188" height="72" rx="18" fill="#111113" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,.12)" />
      <text x="642" y="157" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600">Optional lyric lookup</text>
      <text x="642" y="176" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a8a93" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="9.5">title · artist · album · duration</text>

      <rect x="548" y="222" width="188" height="72" rx="18" fill="#111113" stroke="rgba(255,255,255,.12)" />
      <text x="642" y="251" text-anchor="middle" fill="#fff" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600">Optional update check</text>
      <text x="642" y="270" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8a8a93" font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="9.5">app version only</text>

      <path d="M204 166H278" stroke="#8a8a93" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <path d="M486 136C514 120 520 82 540 74" fill="none" stroke="#8a8a93" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <path d="M486 166H540" stroke="#8a8a93" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
      <path d="M486 198C514 212 520 248 540 254" fill="none" stroke="#8a8a93" stroke-width="1.2" marker-end="url(#arrow)" />
    </svg>
    <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">
      The app's default path: player → your PC → local cache. The two right-hand arrows are optional
      features you can turn off. Lyric lookups send track metadata, not a listening history.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>What stays on your PC</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Settings and window position.</strong> Your style, display, colours, hotkeys and offsets live in your local app-data folder.</li>
    <li><strong>Lyric cache.</strong> Timed lyrics are cached so repeat plays load instantly. You can delete the cache at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>License key and optional Spotify tokens.</strong> These are stored in Windows Credential Manager, not in a plain text file.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What leaves your PC</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Lyric lookups.</strong> When you play a track, Lyrica sends the title, artist, album and
    duration to the lyric provider so it can find timed words. The default is LRCLIB. If you enable
    another provider, its own privacy terms apply. The result is cached locally. Lyrica does not
    send your listening history in bulk.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Update checks.</strong> If update checks are on, Lyrica sends the app version and asks
    whether a newer build exists. It does not send a user ID or listening data. You can turn update
    checks off in Settings.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Features you turn on.</strong> Optional Spotify controls and any future online feature
    only make the requests needed for that feature. They are off until you enable them.
  </p>

  <h2>Spotify and Apple Music account linking</h2>
  <p>
    Spotify linking is optional and is used for playback controls, not for lyrics. If you link it,
    Spotify returns an access token and basic account information; the token is stored in Windows
    Credential Manager and refreshed as needed. Lyrica never receives your Spotify password.
  </p>
  <p>
    To disconnect, open <strong>Settings → Players → Spotify</strong> and choose
    <strong>Disconnect</strong>. That removes the local token. You can also revoke Lyrica's access
    from your Spotify account's connected-apps page. Lyrics keep working through the Windows media
    session after disconnecting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Apple Music and Cider are read through the Windows media session. There is no Apple Music
    account link and no Cider password stored. The Apple Music app does not expose its queue, so
    Lyrica cannot show upcoming tracks from it.
  </p>

  <h2>The website and Discord</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses Discord sign-in only when you choose to sign in, to gate the installer and issue
    one free key. Discord returns your user ID, username, display name and avatar reference. We
    request the <code>identify</code> scope only: no email, password, friends, messages or servers.
  </p>
  <p>
    We store your Discord user ID, the name written into the key, the key itself and the issue time.
    The session cookie is HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax and Secure in production. Signing out clears it.
    To delete the key record, email us with the key or the Discord username on the account. We may
    need to verify that the request is yours.
  </p>
  <p>
    Hosting logs may include an IP address, browser user agent, requested URL and time for security
    and reliability. They are not used for advertising profiles. Analytics are off by default; if
    enabled, the configured provider is cookie-free.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    There are no advertising or analytics cookies. The only cookies are the short-lived OAuth state
    cookie used during Discord sign-in and the session cookie that keeps you signed in. The session
    lasts up to 30 days; signing out clears it.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use the app without signing in to this website (the app itself needs no account).</li>
    <li>Turn off update checks and any optional online provider in Settings.</li>
    <li>Disconnect optional Spotify linking at any time.</li>
    <li>Sign out of the site, or ask us to delete your key record.</li>
    <li>Ask what we hold, correct it, or request a portable copy where the law provides it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to restrict or object to processing,
    or to complain to your local data-protection authority. We would appreciate the chance to
    resolve it first.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is not directed to children under 13. Discord has its own minimum age. If you believe
    a child under 13 has created an account record, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy and will post the new version here with a new date. Material changes
    will be highlighted where practical. Privacy questions or deletion requests:
    <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.legal.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.legal.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>
  <p>See also the <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>.</p>
</TextPage>
